# Patterns are relative to the build context root. Docker uses Go's
# filepath.Match, where `*` does NOT cross `/` — so `*.docx` matches only the
# assignment brief at the root, not the corpus. That distinction is too subtle
# to rely on for a file that decides whether the knowledge base makes it into
# the image, so the corpus is re-included explicitly at the bottom.

# --- version control / tooling state ---
.git
.gitignore
.claude/
.playwright-mcp/

# --- python ---
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- secrets: never in a build context ---
.env
.env.local
*.key

# --- build artefacts ---
# A stale index built with someone else's embedding provider. The image bakes
# its own in the `index` stage.
data/
eval/results/*.json

# --- docs and generated files, not needed at runtime ---
docs/
*.md
/docs/*.pdf
*.png

# --- the assignment brief at the repo root (not the corpus) ---
*.docx

# --- always keep the knowledge base, whatever the rules above say ---
# Later rules win, so this guarantees the corpus reaches the image regardless of
# how the extension patterns are interpreted.
!KnwoledgeBaseDocuments/**
